      en: "Pintianshan (Mount Pintian) is a mountain in Hualien County, Taiwan, part of the Central Mountain Range. It has an elevation of 3,132 meters. The mountain is known for its lush forests and diverse wildlife. The area is an important habitat for the Formosan sika deer (Cervus nippon taiwanensis). The ascent is moderate, passing through dense cloud forests rich in mosses and ferns. Pintianshan lies within Yushan National Park and is popular among birdwatchers. The summit offers a good view of the Yushan massif.",
