      en: "Taipingshan (Mount Taiping) is a mountain in Yilan County, Taiwan, part of the Central Mountain Range. It has an elevation of 1,914 meters. The mountain is known for its scenic forests, misty landscapes, and seas of clouds. Taipingshan is a popular tourist and hiking destination, with well-maintained trails and viewing platforms. The mountain hosts Taipingshan National Forest, famous for its ancient cypress trees. The area is rich in animal and plant species. Snowfall can occur in winter. Taipingshan is also an important forestry area.",
