      en: "Dulanshan (Mount Dulan) is a mountain in Taitung County, Taiwan, part of the Coastal Mountain Range. It has an elevation of 1,062 meters. The mountain is known for its significance in the culture of the indigenous Amis people. Dulanshan is a popular site for paragliding, offering stunning views of the Pacific coast. The area is rich in tropical rainforest and hosts many bird species. The mountain lies in the Dulan Forest Reserve. The climb to the summit takes about 2-3 hours. Dulanshan is also known for its hot springs.",
