      en: "Shitoushan (Lion's Head Mountain) is a mountain in Miaoli County, Taiwan, with an elevation of 492 meters. It is known for its shape that resembles a sitting lion. Shitoushan is a popular spot for hiking and picnics. The area is densely forested and houses many temples and shrines. The mountain is part of the Shitoushan National Scenic Area. The climb is easy, taking about one hour. The summit offers a nice view of the surrounding landscape.",
